string automation.resolveDealPipeline(string dealIdStr)
{
	// =========================================================================
	// _util_resolveDealPipeline   (VERSION: v6-deal-pipeline)
	//
	// THE single authority for a Deal's relationship Pipeline. Reads Deals.Pipeline
	// itself, over REST.
	//
	//   "B2B"          -> B2B relationship. Cadence dispatches.
	//   "Partnership"  -> Partnership. Cadence is held (silently -- an expected state).
	//   "unresolved"   -> the Pipeline could not be read or is not one of the two live
	//                     values. NEVER treated as B2B.
	//
	// ⚠ WORK ITEM 3.1. Two things were wrong here and both are corrected:
	//
	// 1. The Deal_Product_Key route is DELETED. Pipeline was derived from the Product
	//    ("Product Interest is authoritative for the pipeline"), which is a Product-Deal
	//    artefact: under the approved model a Product is a QUOTE under the one Deal, so
	//    a Deal has no Product identity to derive anything from. Pipeline is a property
	//    of the Account RELATIONSHIP and lives on the Deal.
	//
	// 2. The claim that Deals.Pipeline is "UNREADABLE inside the Deluge runtime
	//    (verified 2026-07-16)" was FALSE. Native zoho.crm.getRecordById does omit the
	//    special Pipeline field -- that part is true and is why this helper exists at
	//    all -- but a plain REST GET with ?fields=Pipeline returns it, and it is
	//    populated on 96/96 live Deals. The old comment generalised one API's omission
	//    into a property of the field.
	//
	// ⚠ The failure mode also changed. This used to return "" for an unresolved
	// pipeline, and every caller guarded `if(pipeline != "")` -- which left the mirror
	// blank but let DISPATCH proceed, because the dispatch gate tested `!= "B2B"` and a
	// blank is not B2B... in one place, while pipelineForProductKey("") returned "B2B"
	// and failed OPEN in another. Returning the explicit token "unresolved" makes the
	// two behaviours impossible to confuse: callers that stamp a mirror field must skip
	// it, and callers that gate dispatch must block.
	//
	// Requires the zoho_crm connection (ZohoCRM.modules.deals scope). A connection
	// failure returns "unresolved", never a guess.
	// =========================================================================
	dealId = 0;
	cleanDealId = ifnull(dealIdStr, "").toString().replaceAll("zcrm_", "").trim();
	if(cleanDealId != "" && cleanDealId.matches("[0-9]+")) { dealId = cleanDealId.toLong(); }
	if(dealId == 0) { return "unresolved"; }

	pl = "";
	restHdr = Map();
	restHdr.put("Content-Type", "application/json");
	restResp = invokeurl
	[
		url: "https://www.zohoapis.eu/crm/v6/Deals/" + dealId.toString() + "?fields=Pipeline"
		type: GET
		connection: "zoho_crm"
		headers: restHdr
	];
	if(!isNull(restResp) && restResp.toString().startsWith("{") && !isNull(restResp.get("data")) && restResp.get("data").size() > 0)
	{
		d0 = restResp.get("data").get(0);
		if(!isNull(d0)) { pl = ifnull(d0.get("Pipeline"), "").toString().trim(); }
	}

	// Exactly two live pipelines. Anything else -- blank, "-None-", an unreadable
	// response, a value added to the picklist without updating this authority -- is
	// unresolved, and the caller decides what to do about it.
	if(pl == "B2B" || pl == "Partnership")
	{
		automation.logAutomationEvent("resolveDealPipeline", "Deals", dealId.toString(), "pipeline_resolved", pl, {"via":"deals_pipeline_rest"});
		return pl;
	}

	automation.logAutomationEvent("resolveDealPipeline", "Deals", dealId.toString(), "pipeline_unresolved", "unresolved", {"raw":pl, "resp":ifnull(restResp, "").toString()});
	return "unresolved";
}
